<span class="label">8.</span><cite>Huyghe JR, et al.  Exome array analysis identifies new loci and low-frequency variants influencing insulin processing and secretion. Nature Genetics. 2012 doi: 10.1038/ng.2507. doi:10.1038/ng.2507.</cite> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.2507" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>] [<a href="/articles/PMC3727235/" class="usa-link">PMC free article</a>] [<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23263489/" class="usa-link">PubMed</a>] [<a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Nature%20Genetics&amp;title=Exome%20array%20analysis%20identifies%20new%20loci%20and%20low-frequency%20variants%20influencing%20insulin%20processing%20and%20secretion&amp;author=JR%20Huyghe&amp;publication_year=2012&amp;pmid=23263489&amp;doi=10.1038/ng.2507&amp;" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>]</li>
<li id="R9">
<span class="label">9.</span><cite>Li B, Leal SM. Methods for detecting associations with rare variants for common diseases: application to analysis of sequence data. Am. J. Hum. Genet. 2008;83:311–321. doi: 10.1016/j.ajhg.2008.06.024.</cite> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajhg.2008.06.024" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>] [<a href="/articles/PMC2842185/" class="usa-link">PMC free article</a>] [<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18691683/" class="usa-link">PubMed</a>] [<a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Am.%20J.%20Hum.%20Genet&amp;title=Methods%20for%20detecting%20associations%20with%20rare%20variants%20for%20common%20diseases:%20application%20to%20analysis%20of%20sequence%20data&amp;author=B%20Li&amp;author=SM%20Leal&amp;volume=83&amp;publication_year=2008&amp;pages=311-321&amp;pmid=18691683&amp;doi=10.1016/j.ajhg.2008.06.024&amp;" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>]</li>
<li id="R10">
